# Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3 -- Marco's oracle, and the non-reasoning baseline.
#
# No <think> block: answers are ~2 tokens, so the batch can be far larger than
# the 32B's, and 13.5 GB in bf16 fits one card, which removes NCCL entirely.
#
# MAX_NEW_TOKENS is NOT just a speed knob. 32 was tried on job 4064797 and ~1.5%
# of answers hit the cap: Mistral mostly answers in two tokens but sometimes
# explains itself first, and a capped answer is scored from whatever text fits,
# or falls back to False when no True/False appears at all. Generation stops at
# EOS, so headroom costs nothing on the answers that do not need it.
#
# Marco served this through Ollama, which defaults to 4-bit Q4_0; this runs
# bf16. Same weights, different numerics -- a baseline, not a reproduction.
#
# The weight directory needs two fields added to config.json by hand:
#   partial_rotary_factor = 1.0
#   head_dim              = hidden_size / num_attention_heads   (4096/32 = 128)
# transformers 4.57 defines both as None and vLLM 0.8.2 multiplies them, so
# without these the engine dies in llama.py before loading. Re-downloading the
# model reverts them.
MODEL_DIR="models/mistral-7b-instruct-v0.3"
MODEL_NAME="mistral"
TENSOR_PARALLEL=1
GPUS="a100:1"
MAX_NEW_TOKENS=128
EXACTLEARNER_BATCH_SIZE=256
